WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.300
Start with ethanoic acid.

2
00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:05.600
It is a weak acid, sharp and sour.

3
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:08.880
Now swap one of its hydrogens
for a carbon group.

4
00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:12.860
The new molecule is methyl
ethanoate, an ester.

5
00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:15.780
Esters are used in perfumes and in food.

6
00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:20.960
A single small swap, and a sour acid
becomes a sweet-smelling liquid.

7
00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:23.940
How can one hydrogen matter that much?

8
00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:29.900
In this mission, you'll make esters by warming
acids with alcohols and an acid catalyst.

9
00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:31.880
Then you'll split esters apart again,

10
00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:36.380
using hot acid or hot alkali,
and compare what you get.

11
00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:42.840
Your mission: explain how swapping one hydrogen
turns a sour acid into a sweet-smelling ester.